The interesting ones are marked with an asterisk.

Note that I got unknown spells from the appropriate classes only at first.
I didn't get any duplicate spells, only spells that I didn't know yet.

The first exception to this "rule" was a blank spellbook, but that's
excusable, since it might still be useful to write a spell from an
appropriate class.

The second exception was the duplicate spellbook of invisibility. At that
point, I didn't have detect treasure yet, so I guess the game tried to
give me an unknown spell for a certain number of tries, and failed, after
which it gave me a random spellbook which happened to be from one of my
three classes.

The third exception was the spellbook of cancellation, which was the first
spellbook I got from an unknown spell class (matter spells). After I read
